  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 101 PM CDT Thu Aug 20 2026\n\nWeak cold front continues to generate a few showers and storms\nacross Oklahoma north of the Red River. Given the northerly flow\naloft on the eastern edge of the upper level high, a little of\nthis mid level moisture will try to work its way south for\ntomorrow and Saturday, perhaps aided by a couple weak shortwaves\nrotating through as well. Upper ridge will remain strong, but \nseveral of the CAMs (RRFS, FV3) try to generate a few showers and \nstorms across the area. Given some consistency with this idea over\nthe last few days, will add some mentionable 10% POPs across\nportions of the Big Country and Heartland for Friday and Saturday\nevenings. \n\nAfter that, center of the upper ridge shifts a little farther east\nand temperatures heat up even more for early/middle of next week.\nNo rain in sight, at least in any meaningful way and not much to\nsuggest that the 100 degree days will stop even into next weekend.",
